scene: The grazers, walkers and the wood's keepers have spent a winter agreeing rules for the common: when the sheep go up, which paths rest each spring, who mends the walls. The council says it cannot recognise a forum it did not set up, and the sheep go up in a month. {N} has heard about {aim.round}.
scene tribal: The herders of four camps have agreed their own customs for the shared grazing, season by season. The elders say a gathering of herders has no standing at the moot. The flocks go up in a moon, and {N} has heard about {aim.round}.
scene magic: The commoners of the heath have agreed rules for grazing, cutting and burning. The steward says an assembly without a charter cannot be heard. The flocks go out at the spring quarter, and {N} has heard about {aim.round}.
