- U>B | hold off a season, and see whether a better offer comes once it spreads | v: self-direction, power | aim: ease | foot: door turned down a chance | chance: 78
- B>R | play the firm against its biggest rival, and take whichever pays most | v: power, stimulation | aim: take | foot: person rival | chance: 57
- R>G | refuse, and start a makers' cooperative to build it openly together | v: stimulation, benevolence | aim: try | foot: person friend | chance: 60
- G>W | take a fair fee for advice only, and leave the plans where they are | v: benevolence, conformity | aim: take | foot: lesson a fair price for help | chance: 62
