scene: Every month {N} sits down with two sets of numbers: the accounts and the land's own readings, soil, water, hedges, birds. For the first time this spring they are on the same table, and the question is plain. Which parts of the business pay their way because they spend the land, and which pay because they mend it? The next month's figures are due on Friday.
scene tribal: Every moon {N} counts the grass and the springs beside the herd, as if they were wealth too. This spring the two counts sit side by side for the first time, and they do not always agree.
scene magic: {N} has had the soil and water of the estate written into the steward's ledger beside the coin. This month, for the first time, the two columns sit side by side, and the steward has questions.
- W | keep both sets of books to the same strict standard, every month without fail | v: conformity, security | aim: work | foot: lesson two ledgers, one standard | chance: 78
- U | find the one line in the business where profit and renewal pull hardest apart | v: self-direction, universalism | aim: work | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 68
- B | price the land's improvement in, and show buyers what they are paying for | v: achievement, power | aim: work | foot: means money+.04 | chance: 67
- R | drop the product that spends the land most, this month, and see what happens | v: stimulation, universalism | aim: work | foot: mark took a wild risk | chance: 57
- G | keep the books simple, and spend more time out on the land itself | v: tradition, benevolence | aim: ease | foot: place prod.land | chance: 77
- W>B | show both sets of numbers to the bank, and argue the firm is worth more | v: conformity, power | aim: work | foot: person colleague | chance: 60
- U>R | try three small changes on three fields, and compare them by the autumn | v: self-direction, stimulation | aim: work | foot: lesson small trials, clear answers | chance: 68
- B>G | share the readings with the neighbouring farms, and buy from those who mend their land | v: achievement, benevolence | aim: work | foot: person neighbour | chance: 70
- R>W | walk the land with the whole staff each month, numbers in hand | v: stimulation, conformity | aim: work | foot: means ties+.04 | chance: 77
- G>U | skip the figures one month, and just watch the land through a season | v: security, self-direction | aim: ease | foot: means health+.03 | chance: 77
works: The two sets of numbers start telling one story, and {N} can see where the business is headed.
works: Month by month it becomes a habit, and the land and the accounts both get a little better.
fails: The numbers disagree in ways nobody can explain, and the month ends in more questions.
fails: The extra work piles up, and for a while the readings fall behind.

