magic: {N} leads the college's first survey of the far valley, and every night the day's findings must be set down
scene: Nobody has mapped the far valley properly, and {N} is leading the first survey: six weeks, a small team, a pack each. The rule {N} has set is simple and hard: every night, however tired, the day's findings are written up and sent back before anyone sleeps. Two weeks in, the team is tired, and the valley keeps showing them things nobody has seen.
scene tribal: Nobody has walked the far valley in living memory, and {N} leads the first walk in. Every night the day's finds are told at the fire and remembered word for word. Two weeks in, everyone is tired, and the valley keeps showing them new things.
scene magic: The far valley has never been surveyed, and {N} leads the college's first company in. Every night the day's findings are set down and sent back by bird. Two weeks in, the company is weary and the valley keeps surprising them.
